{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Th8j5d92mmqZBqvBhY2fHy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings, plain-text source of truth).\n\n- **Purpose â€” task/project management over markdown.** It tracks tasks and projects across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) where the markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) *are* the database â€” no DB, no lock files, Python stdlib only.\n\n- **What it ships #1 â€” a local web dashboard (`anchor_gui.py`, the declared deliverable).** A self-contained stdlib HTTP server that regenerates the full dashboard HTML on each request, binds `http://localhost:8777`, and writes changes straight back to the markdown files. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (not launched by hand). Tasks move through a lifecycle: active â†’ done / cancelled / saved-for-later / restored.\n\n- **What it ships #2 â€” a CLI mirror (`anchor.py`).** Same logic as the GUI plus static `dashboard.html` generation; commands like `done`, `add`, `capture`, `cancel`, `save`, `restore`, and an `rnd` inspection mirror.\n\n- **What it ships #3 â€” a daily self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`).** Runs 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler; verifies file integrity, exercises every endpoint on a throwaway port, walks a synthetic task through all states, and walks the R&D v2/v3/v4 surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`), writing `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n\n- **What it ships #4 â€” an R&D \"Project Cockpit\" control surface (v4, the major recent build).** Turns each project's window into mission-control for the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** trio: per-lane tiles with a single honest status light (green/amber/red/grey), inline expanding panels (summary + a real resizable terminal), cached/validated session & project summaries, a cost/tokens/time rollup, a grass-idea board, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Terminal substrate.** Real Windows **ConPTY** terminals via the *one* declared native exception, `pywinpty` (lazy import, `pty_manager.py` only, optional `[terminal]` extra) â€” rendered with xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE transport, with per-session git-worktree isolation. The lane's trio skill auto-loads once and greets once (the v4 fix for the old repeating-prompt bug). Everything else stays stdlib; the dashboard works even if `pywinpty` is absent.\n\n- **Branding.** Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\", using the vendored brand mark as favicon and masthead lockup.\n\nThe R&D v4 surface was built by Foreman (9 waves GREEN, 637 tests passed) and merged to master on 2026-06-13 (merge `38fd70e`); deploy is `nssm restart anchor` (elevated)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4251,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4251,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d66d1800-a802-4e34-9814-0e6d2e894efd","uuid":"e397228d-e2cc-429e-ad2a-1cb75fb783fb","request_id":"req_011Cc1JVr9wDsQe6tHaP4Ceh"}
